-- ccc32-related-3.l4 -- the related provisions of amending Acts, 2024 to 2026, from the end of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46
-- (lines 19376-19516 of the text: 2024, c. 22, s. 8; 2024, c. 23, s. 13; 2026, c. 11, ss. 56 to 58; 2026, c. 12, ss. 15 and 16; 2026, c. 15, s. 11.1; 2026, c. 19, ss. 87 and 96 to 118).
-- Part ccc32, layer 1. How a result reads, the naming rule and the rule for the days commencement leaves open: see the head of ccc32-related-1.l4 and NOTES.md.
-- 2026, c. 19 defines its own commencement day (section 96): the 30th day after the day on which it receives royal assent. Every function that turns on it takes the day of royal assent
-- as an input and computes the commencement day with `2026 c 19 s 96 commencement day`; the day of royal assent is not in the sources.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text,
-- and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.

§ `2024, c. 22, s. 8 -- an information under subsection 810(1) deemed laid under subsection 810.03(1)`

-- 8 If an information has been laid under 810(1) before the day this Act comes into force by a person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence that will cause personal injury to the intimate partner or a child
-- of the other person, or to a child of the other person's intimate partner, and a provincial court judge has not made a final determination with respect to the information, the information is deemed, on that day, to have been laid under 810.03(1).
-- "intimate partner" is the section 2 term: its answer is an input carried through as a MAYBE BOOLEAN (it can be NOT COVERED). A failed "if" is the text's no within the provision (marginal reading).
-- src:19377 | 8 If an information has been laid under subsection 810(1) of the Criminal Code before the day on which this Act comes into force by a person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence that will cause personal injury to the intimate partner or a child of the other person, or to a child of the other person’s intimate partner, and a provincial court judge has not made a final determination with respect to the information, the information is deemed, on that day, to have been laid under subsection 810.03(1) of that Act.
@ref 2024, c. 22, s. 8 (src:19377)
GIVEN `the day on which 2024, c. 22 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the information was laid under subsection 810(1)` IS A DATE
      `the information was laid by a person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence that will cause personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 intimate partner: the person at risk is the other person’s intimate partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person at risk is a child of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 intimate partner: the person at risk is a child of the other person’s intimate partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a provincial court judge has not made a final determination with respect to the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 22 s 8 the information is deemed to have been laid under subsection 810.03(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the day the information was laid under subsection 810(1)` LESS THAN `the day on which 2024, c. 22 comes into force`
                AND `the information was laid by a person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence that will cause personal injury`
                AND `a provincial court judge has not made a final determination with respect to the information`)
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an information has been laid under subsection 810(1) of the Criminal Code before the day on which this Act comes into force"
        IF `the person at risk is within the class` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person at risk is within the class` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an intimate partner is for section 2 "intimate partner", whose answer is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "personal injury to the intimate partner or a child of the other person, or to a child of the other person’s intimate partner"
    WHERE
        `the person at risk is within the class` MEANS
            IF `s 2 intimate partner: the person at risk is the other person’s intimate partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
               OR `the person at risk is a child of the other person`
               OR `s 2 intimate partner: the person at risk is a child of the other person’s intimate partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE IF `s 2 intimate partner: the person at risk is the other person’s intimate partner` EQUALS NOTHING
                    OR `s 2 intimate partner: the person at risk is a child of the other person’s intimate partner` EQUALS NOTHING
                 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an intimate partner is for section 2 "intimate partner", whose answer is not covered
                 ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "personal injury to the intimate partner or a child of the other person, or to a child of the other person’s intimate partner"

§ `2024, c. 23, s. 13 -- proceedings and documents related to section 163.1 are not invalidated by the change of name`

-- 13 The amendments made by this Act do not affect the validity of any proceedings, brought under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, that are related to section 163.1 and are ongoing on the day this Act comes into force.
-- The amendments do not affect the validity of any document related to those proceedings and any reference to child pornography in such a document is to be read as a reference to child sexual abuse and exploitation material.
-- src:19380 | Proceedings not invalid
-- src:19381 | 13 The amendments made by this Act do not affect the validity of any proceedings, brought under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, that are related to section 163.1 of the Criminal Code and are ongoing on the day on which this Act comes into force. The amendments do not affect the validity of any document related to those proceedings and any reference to “child pornography” in such a document is to be read as a reference to “child sexual abuse and exploitation material”.
@ref 2024, c. 23, s. 13 (src:19380-19381)
GIVEN `the proceedings are brought under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are related to section 163.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are ongoing on the day on which 2024, c. 23 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 23 s 13 the amendments made by 2024, c. 23 affect the validity of the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are brought under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament` AND `the proceedings are related to section 163.1` AND `the proceedings are ongoing on the day on which 2024, c. 23 comes into force`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The amendments made by this Act do not affect the validity of any proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that are related to section 163.1 of the Criminal Code and are ongoing on the day on which this Act comes into force"

@ref 2024, c. 23, s. 13 (src:19380-19381)
GIVEN `the document is related to proceedings that are brought under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, are related to section 163.1 and are ongoing on the day on which 2024, c. 23 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 23 s 13 the amendments made by 2024, c. 23 affect the validity of the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is related to proceedings that are brought under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, are related to section 163.1 and are ongoing on the day on which 2024, c. 23 comes into force`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The amendments do not affect the validity of any document related to those proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any document related to those proceedings"

@ref 2024, c. 23, s. 13 (src:19380-19381)
GIVEN `the document is related to proceedings that are brought under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, are related to section 163.1 and are ongoing on the day on which 2024, c. 23 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference in the document is to child pornography` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`2024 c 23 s 13 the reference to child pornography in the document is read as a reference to` MEANS
    IF `the document is related to proceedings that are brought under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, are related to section 163.1 and are ongoing on the day on which 2024, c. 23 comes into force` AND `the reference in the document is to child pornography`
    THEN JUST "child sexual abuse and exploitation material"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reference to “child pornography” in such a document"

§ `2026, c. 11, ss. 56 to 58 -- outstanding fines and offences committed after commencement`

-- 56 Unless the context requires otherwise, words and expressions used in sections 57 and 58 have the same meaning as in the Criminal Code. A pointer: the meaning is the Code's (another part), taken as an input.
-- src:19384 | Words and expressions
-- src:19385 | 56 Unless the context requires otherwise, words and expressions used in sections 57 and 58 have the same meaning as in the Criminal Code.
@ref 2026, c. 11, s. 56 (src:19384-19385)
GIVEN `the word or expression is used in section 57 or 58 of 2026, c. 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context requires otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 the word or expression is within the meaning it has in the Criminal Code` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2026 c 11 s 56 the word or expression has the same meaning as in the Criminal Code` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the word or expression is used in section 57 or 58 of 2026, c. 11` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "words and expressions used in sections 57 and 58"
        IF `the context requires otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the context requires otherwise"
        OTHERWISE `s 2 the word or expression is within the meaning it has in the Criminal Code`

-- 57 The provisions of the Code, as enacted by sections 41 and 42, apply to the proceeds of a fine that is unpaid on the day those sections come into force.
