§ `2026, c. 15, s. 11.1 -- clarification: statements on matters of public interest (subsections 319(2), (2.1) and (2.2))`

-- 11.1 (1) For greater certainty, nothing in 319(2) or (2.2) shall be construed as prohibiting a person from communicating a statement on a matter of public interest, including an educational, religious, political or scientific statement made in the course of
-- a discussion, publication or debate, if they do not wilfully promote hatred against an identifiable group by communicating the statement.
-- Named for the protection the clarification gives, never for a prohibition. A failed "if" is the text's no for THIS CLARIFICATION only (marginal reading): whether section 319 itself prohibits the statement is for section 319 (part ccc10).
-- src:19408 | Clarification — subsections 319(2) and (2.2)
-- src:19409 | 11.1 (1) For greater certainty, nothing in subsection 319(2) or (2.2) of the Criminal Code shall be construed as prohibiting a person from communicating a statement on a matter of public interest, including an educational, religious, political or scientific statement made in the course of a discussion, publication or debate, if they do not wilfully promote hatred against an identifiable group by communicating the statement.
@ref 2026, c. 15, s. 11.1(1) (src:19408-19409)
GIVEN `the statement is a statement on a matter of public interest, including an educational, religious, political or scientific statement made in the course of a discussion, publication or debate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not wilfully promote hatred against an identifiable group by communicating the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2026 c 15 s 11.1(1) the clarification applies to the person's communication of the statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the statement is a statement on a matter of public interest, including an educational, religious, political or scientific statement made in the course of a discussion, publication or debate` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "communicating a statement on a matter of public interest, including an educational, religious, political or scientific statement made in the course of a discussion, publication or debate"
        IF NOT `the person does not wilfully promote hatred against an identifiable group by communicating the statement` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if they do not wilfully promote hatred against an identifiable group by communicating the statement"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

