-- 2026 c 19 s 105: "applies only" -- on or after the commencement day is within the limit (JUST TRUE); before it, the text says no (JUST FALSE).
-- src:19452 | Part XV.1
-- src:19453 | 105 For greater certainty, Part XV.1 of the Act applies only with respect to an offence that is committed on or after the commencement day.
@ref 2026, c. 19, s. 105 (src:19452-19453)
GIVEN `the day on which 2026, c. 19 receives royal assent` IS A DATE
      `the day the offence was committed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2026 c 19 s 105 the offence is within the time limit on Part XV.1` MEANS
    IF `the day the offence was committed` AT LEAST (`2026 c 19 s 96 commencement day` `the day on which 2026, c. 19 receives royal assent`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applies only with respect to an offence that is committed on or after the commencement day"


