-- 2026 c 19 s 110: a grant limited to orders made before the commencement day: before it is JUST TRUE; any other order is outside the grant's own wording (NOTHING).
-- src:19472 | Revocation or variation of order — non-publication
-- src:19473 | 110 Section 672.5011 of the Act applies with respect to orders that are made under section 672.501 of the Act before commencement day.
@ref 2026, c. 19, s. 110 (src:19472-19473)
GIVEN `the day on which 2026, c. 19 receives royal assent` IS A DATE
      `the day the order was made under section 672.501` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2026 c 19 s 110 section 672.5011 applies to the order` MEANS
    IF `the day the order was made under section 672.501` LESS THAN (`2026 c 19 s 96 commencement day` `the day on which 2026, c. 19 receives royal assent`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies with respect to orders that are made under section 672.501 of the Act before commencement day"


-- 111 (1) An alternative measure used in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence under any of sections 717 to 717.4, as those sections read before the commencement day,
-- is deemed, on or after the commencement day, to be an alternative measure, as defined in section 715.44. "on or after the commencement day": before it, the text says no.
-- src:19476 | Alternative measure
-- src:19477 | 111 (1) An alternative measure used in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence under any of sections 717 to 717.4 of the Act, as those sections read before the commencement day, is deemed, on or after the commencement day, to be an alternative measure, as defined in section 715.44 of the Act.
@ref 2026, c. 19, s. 111(1) (src:19476-19477)
GIVEN `the day on which 2026, c. 19 receives royal assent` IS A DATE
      `the day the question is about` IS A DATE
      `the alternative measure was used in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence under any of sections 717 to 717.4, as those sections read before the commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2026 c 19 s 111(1) the measure is deemed to be an alternative measure, as defined in section 715.44` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the alternative measure was used in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence under any of sections 717 to 717.4, as those sections read before the commencement day` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An alternative measure used in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence under any of sections 717 to 717.4 of the Act, as those sections read before the commencement day"
        IF `the day the question is about` LESS THAN (`2026 c 19 s 96 commencement day` `the day on which 2026, c. 19 receives royal assent`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed, on or after the commencement day"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

