-- 115 Section 740.1 applies only with respect to an order referred to in section 732.1 or 742.3, as that section read on commencement day, in respect of an offence that is committed on or after that day.
-- src:19494 | Restitution order
-- src:19495 | 115 For greater certainty, section 740.1 of the Act applies only with respect to an order referred to in section 732.1 or 742.3 of the Act, as that section read on commencement day, in respect of an offence that is committed on or after that day.
@ref 2026, c. 19, s. 115 (src:19494-19495)
GIVEN `the day on which 2026, c. 19 receives royal assent` IS A DATE
      `the order is an order referred to in section 732.1 or 742.3, as that section read on commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the offence was committed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2026 c 19 s 115 the order is within the limits on section 740.1` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order is an order referred to in section 732.1 or 742.3, as that section read on commencement day` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applies only with respect to an order referred to in section 732.1 or 742.3 of the Act"
        IF `the day the offence was committed` AT LEAST (`2026 c 19 s 96 commencement day` `the day on which 2026, c. 19 receives royal assent`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of an offence that is committed on or after that day"

